# (AI-assisted) Jak II: from the title screen into Haven City gameplay (the slums, with traffic).
# docs/3ds-port/jak2_status.md "Scripted route and memory survey". Native PC or C mode, e.g.
#   OPENGOAL_NO_SOUND=1 OPENGOAL_NULL_GFX_FPS=30 OPENGOAL_PAD_SCRIPT=jak2_city.pad \
#     gk -g jak2 --proj-path <project> --null-gfx -- -boot -fakeiso -nosound
# "continue" starts a new game (speedrun act-2 task state) at that continue point from anywhere,
# title screen included (goal_src/jak2/pc/features/speedruns.gc pad-script-continue).
# Frames below count game frames; "wait" stops the clock until Jak stands (levels loaded).
1000 continue ctysluma-start
1001 -
1002 wait *target* target-stance
1003 log city: ctysluma-start
1004 pos *target*
# let traffic spawn (citizens, guards, vehicles), then the memory report
1400 print *pad-script-mem*
# timing windows (platform/3ds/tools/perf_report.py): city-stand = 600 frames standing in the
# slums with traffic around; city-walk = 300 frames walking forward (ends against a wall)
1401 log perf-mark city-stand
2000 log perf-mark city-walk
2001 ly=0
2300 -
2301 log perf-mark end
2302 pos *target*
2303 print *target*
2400 exit
